{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#149","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#149","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#149\",\"parent_revision\":\"f72081b138260b1523d1069dcdfad56ceb88ea13e04783b850a2cec1b44ebc2c\",\"root_revision\":\"f72081b138260b1523d1069dcdfad56ceb88ea13e04783b850a2cec1b44ebc2c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`packages/skilllint/frontmatter_core.py:203` types `AgentFrontmatter.skills` as `object | None`.\\n\\n`docs/TYPING_POLICY.md` \u00a73 forbids a broad `object`/`Any` field outside boundary modules, and `frontmatter_core.py` does not match the approved boundary naming conventions (`*_validators.py`, `*_boundary.py`, or `packages/skilllint/boundary/`).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why It Is Not Urgent\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nVerified during review of #147:\\n\\n- Nothing downstream reads `.skills` directly. The only consumer is the model's own `normalized_skills: list[str]` property (`frontmatter_core.py:216-218`), confirmed by `grep -rn \\\"\\\\.skills\\\\b\\\"`.\\n- `uv run ty check packages/` passes clean.\\n- The same class already carries `mcp_servers: list[Any] | dict[str, Any]` and `hooks: dict[str, Any]`, so this is not a new departure in this file \u2014 which is itself the argument for fixing the file rather than the field.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nReplace the bare `object` with a typed recursive YAML-value alias, and decide whether `frontmatter_core.py` should be declared a typed boundary (which would legitimise the two pre-existing `Any` fields) or brought fully inside the typed core.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #147 \u2014 where this was introduced and reviewed\\n- #41 \u2014 Tier-2 typing cleanup, same family of concern\\n</di